"""
# `iso` capability -- real source-text parse -> HIR -> MIR -> borrow-check pipeline

**Lane:** ISO2 `iso-parse` (2026-07-29)

Completes the real-source-text red-line probe that
`test/01_unit/compiler/borrow/iso_move_pipeline_spec.spl` (LANE ISO1) could
not do: that spec hand-builds HIR because `parse_full_frontend` had zero
construction sites for `TypeKind.Isolated`/`TypeKind.Atomic` (bug:
`doc/08_tracking/bug/iso_mut_capability_prefix_not_parsed_2026-07-29.md`).

This lane (ISO2) wired `iso T` through the real recursive-descent parser:
1. `10.frontend/core/parser.spl` `parser_parse_type_impl` -- a leading `iso`
   identifier (lexed as a plain TOK_IDENT, not a reserved keyword token) now
   registers its inner type in a new side-table (`10.frontend/core/types.spl`
   `isolated_type_register`/`TYPE_ISOLATED_BASE`, mirroring the existing
   Dict<K,V>/Result<T,E>/array-element registries) instead of being consumed
   as an ordinary named type itself.
2. `10.frontend/_FlatAstBridge/convert_nodes.spl` `convert_flat_type` --
   rebuilds the real `TypeKind.Isolated(inner)` from that side-table entry.
3. HIR `lower_type` (`20.hir/hir_lowering/types.spl`) already had a ready
   `HirTypeKind.Isolated` arm from LANE ISO1 -- no change needed there.

`mut T` in the SAME type position (`fn take(a: mut i64) -> i64`) is a
DIFFERENT, still-unimplemented capability: HIR `lower_type` explicitly falls
it (and `TypeKind.Atomic`) into the erased `Infer` catch-all, so there is no
downstream consumer to wire it to yet. Left unhandled by this lane on
purpose -- see the bug doc. (The pre-existing `fn f(mut x: T)` -- `mut`
BEFORE the parameter name, not after the `:` -- is an unrelated, already-
working mechanism: `parser_skip_mut_if_present`/`PARAM_MUTS`, feeding
`HirParam.is_mutable` for by-reference binding. Not the same feature.)

## Harness landmine

The parse -> HIR -> MIR pipeline is inlined in each `it` block on purpose,
mirroring `enum_match_unknown_variant_diagnostic_spec.spl`'s documented
landmine: running the identical code inside a module-level helper fn loses
recorded lowering/checker state when read back afterward. Also uses
`driver_core_compile_options_default()`, never `CompileOptions.default()`
(same erased-receiver resolution failure that spec documents).
"""

use std.spec
use compiler.common.config.Logger
use compiler.frontend.frontend.parse_full_frontend
use compiler.hir.hir_lowering.types.HirLowering
use compiler.hir.hir_lowering.items.*
use compiler.mir.mir.*
use compiler.common.driver_core_types.{driver_core_compile_options_default}
use compiler.driver.driver_mir_target.{driver_mir_target_context}
use compiler.borrow.borrow_check.*

describe "iso use-after-move through the real parser (red-line probe)":
    it "reports a borrow diagnostic for real source text `fn take(a: iso i64) -> i64:` with two place-reads of `a`":
        val src = "fn take(a: iso i64) -> i64:\n" +
            "    val b = a\n" +
            "    val c = a\n" +
            "    0\n"
        val parsed = parse_full_frontend(src, "testdata/fixture_iso_move.spl", "fixture_iso_move", Logger(level: 0))
        var hir_lowering = HirLowering.with_filename("testdata/fixture_iso_move.spl")
        val hir = hir_lowering.lower_module(parsed)
        val target_context = driver_mir_target_context(driver_core_compile_options_default())
        var lowering = MirLowering.new_for_target(hir.symbols, target_context)
        val mir = lowering.lower_module(hir)
        val errors = check_mir_module(mir)
        assert_true(errors.len() > 0)

describe "iso moved then reassigned then used through the real parser (kill-on-reassign)":
    it "reports no borrow diagnostic for real source text when `a` is reassigned before its next use":
        val src = "fn take(a: iso i64) -> i64:\n" +
            "    val b = a\n" +
            "    a = 2\n" +
            "    val c = a\n" +
            "    0\n"
        val parsed = parse_full_frontend(src, "testdata/fixture_iso_reassign.spl", "fixture_iso_reassign", Logger(level: 0))
        var hir_lowering = HirLowering.with_filename("testdata/fixture_iso_reassign.spl")
        val hir = hir_lowering.lower_module(parsed)
        val target_context = driver_mir_target_context(driver_core_compile_options_default())
        var lowering = MirLowering.new_for_target(hir.symbols, target_context)
        val mir = lowering.lower_module(hir)
        val errors = check_mir_module(mir)
        assert_true(errors.len() == 0)

describe "identical real source text without iso is unaffected":
    it "reports no borrow diagnostic for the same shape without `iso` (plain `a: i64`)":
        val src = "fn take(a: i64) -> i64:\n" +
            "    val b = a\n" +
            "    val c = a\n" +
            "    0\n"
        val parsed = parse_full_frontend(src, "testdata/fixture_no_iso.spl", "fixture_no_iso", Logger(level: 0))
        var hir_lowering = HirLowering.with_filename("testdata/fixture_no_iso.spl")
        val hir = hir_lowering.lower_module(parsed)
        val target_context = driver_mir_target_context(driver_core_compile_options_default())
        var lowering = MirLowering.new_for_target(hir.symbols, target_context)
        val mir = lowering.lower_module(hir)
        val errors = check_mir_module(mir)
        assert_true(errors.len() == 0)
